{"title":"Finding where plants get sunlight, water, and air","key_idea":"Plants make their own food by taking three things from different places: sunlight from the sky, water from soil, and air through leaf pores.","method":["Think about where the sun shines — that is where plants get sunlight.","Look at the ground around a plant — water soaks into the soil, and roots drink it up.","Remember that air is all around us — tiny holes in the bottom of leaves called stomata let air (carbon dioxide) enter the plant."],"worked_example":{"problem":"A rice plant in a field needs sunlight, water, and air. Where does each come from?","steps":["The sun is high in the sky above the field, so the rice plant gets sunlight from there.","Rain falls on the ground and water soaks down into the soil where the rice plant's roots can absorb it.","Air surrounds the plant everywhere, and it enters through tiny pores on the leaves."],"answer":"Sunlight comes from the sky, water comes from the soil through roots, and air enters through leaf pores."},"key_terms":[{"term":"stomata","meaning":"tiny holes on leaves that let air move in and out"},{"term":"roots","meaning":"the parts of a plant underground that suck up water from soil"},{"term":"photosynthesis","meaning":"the way plants make food using sunlight, water, and air"}],"common_mistakes":["Thinking plants get water from the air instead of from the soil","Forgetting that air is something plants need, not just animals"],"remember":"Sunlight from sky, water from soil, air through leaf pores — plants gather all three to cook their own food.","quick_check":[{"q":"Where does a plant get the water it needs to make food?","a":"From the soil, which is soaked up by the roots."},{"q":"What part of the leaf lets air enter the plant?","a":"Tiny pores called stomata on the leaf."}],"tell_your_child":"Plants are like little factories with their own kitchen — the sun gives energy, roots drink from the ground, and leaves breathe in air. Can you point to where each of these things comes from on a plant near your home?"}
```
